# Docker matches these against paths relative to the build context root, so a bare
# `data` or `*.db` only ever matched the top level. Every one of those lives *inside* a
# workspace package here (apps/api/data, apps/api/prisma/data), so the unanchored forms
# let ~10 MB of local development databases into the context — and `apps/api/prisma` is
# copied wholesale into the runtime image, which shipped them. Anchor with `**/`.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Local state: developer databases, server working directories, backup archives.
**/data
**/volumes
**/backups
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite*

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/*.log
.DS_Store
# Prose and the installer. `COPY . .` in the build stage would otherwise sweep these into the
# context on every build; nothing in the Dockerfile reads them. LICENSE is deliberately not
# here — a container image should carry its licence.
docs
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
install.sh
